{"schema": "jv-source-correction/1", "record_type": "source_correction", "audit_id": "OLSIZ-20260904", "finding_id": "OLSIZ-005", "status": "applied_and_verified", "source": {"revision": "9620cc73f9c8e0ad003c514a5d3748f29611c4c0", "unit_id": "OLP-0034", "path": "content/sets-functions-relations/size-of-sets/reduction.tex", "bytes": 5540, "sha256": "0d6d2e3280698668b837cef6dcf3134b86d2a4b48831ae516e6e33e42898c79a", "locator": "lines 85-100", "finding": "The displayed h(n) is explicitly a finite string of n zeros, but h is declared to map into the set of infinite binary sequences.", "controlling_evidence": "Membership in Bin^omega requires an infinite binary sequence; appending an infinite tail, for example n zeros followed by ones forever, supplies the intended non-surjective example.", "mathematical_delta": {"display_tail_added": "an explicit infinite tail"}}, "target": {"path": "translation/content/sets-functions-relations/size-of-sets/reduction.tex", "bytes": 5770, "sha256": "11ff639ead636b6bf93c911baac161f576aabc515613b2a043d27eddd769c38f", "adjacent_note_lines": [102], "adjacent_contexts": [{"line_start": 100, "line_end": 103, "sha256_utf8_lf": "4eadfb0288fcd9110cf55f8d0d24a5f84f67250f90689774292b7c4529c065f7"}], "applied_handling": "Replaced the finite zero string by n leading zeros followed by an infinite tail of ones."}, "audit_artifacts": {"findings_file": "FINDINGS.json", "findings_sha256": "9b6e836c8432eb75d331913983603796d6557da6ec3ad71b846b2a248374cd07", "review_file": "REVIEW.md", "review_sha256": "26913176baacbda5ae8a47bcc82ccf0366b0763313e6eeeb45df59e64249a1f9"}, "verification": {"frozen_source_hash_matches_manifest": true, "frozen_source_unmodified": true, "batch_qa_sha256": "05d2bbf0c18ae77157a8bb2a0cafef0e10d1841adbad1eaa8878d4f7a73ec006", "structural_status": "structural_pass", "semantic_review_sha256": "03e91c3b1b5f30b2670a27a14ee56599f5a565408a788c49e2edde48722f3480", "semantic_review_status": "pass"}}
{"schema": "jv-source-correction/1", "record_type": "source_correction", "audit_id": "OLSIZ-20260904", "finding_id": "OLSIZ-006", "status": "applied_and_verified", "source": {"revision": "9620cc73f9c8e0ad003c514a5d3748f29611c4c0", "unit_id": "OLP-0035", "path": "content/sets-functions-relations/size-of-sets/equinumerous-sets.tex", "bytes": 4141, "sha256": "025a3fc368d6873825effcb07631913762edbf2d3f9a0711d57dcd9575361251", "locator": "lines 68-94", "finding": "Two conditional variants refer to g(x)=y before g is introduced, although the bijection in scope is f.", "controlling_evidence": "The proof has fixed f:A to B; g is introduced only later as an enumeration of A.", "mathematical_delta": {"occurrences": 2, "removed": "g(x)=y", "added": "f(x)=y"}}, "target": {"path": "translation/content/sets-functions-relations/size-of-sets/equinumerous-sets.tex", "bytes": 4352, "sha256": "d98271ec9b67b12c13f379e3c616b0fa86312a5ee043621000d0243f8541f66d", "adjacent_note_lines": [75, 92], "adjacent_contexts": [{"line_start": 73, "line_end": 76, "sha256_utf8_lf": "bb8de24cc024f141de2c7a697f9f77034bd9c418c61d03bd727e515b92a09ba4"}, {"line_start": 90, "line_end": 93, "sha256_utf8_lf": "93e718993f2933c12bf6bfadbc98a25e95c5a86f1bc156b5949acc6a07ca1007"}], "applied_handling": "Replaced both premature g(x)=y occurrences by f(x)=y."}, "audit_artifacts": {"findings_file": "FINDINGS.json", "findings_sha256": "9b6e836c8432eb75d331913983603796d6557da6ec3ad71b846b2a248374cd07", "review_file": "REVIEW.md", "review_sha256": "26913176baacbda5ae8a47bcc82ccf0366b0763313e6eeeb45df59e64249a1f9"}, "verification": {"frozen_source_hash_matches_manifest": true, "frozen_source_unmodified": true, "batch_qa_sha256": "05d2bbf0c18ae77157a8bb2a0cafef0e10d1841adbad1eaa8878d4f7a73ec006", "structural_status": "structural_pass", "semantic_review_sha256": "03e91c3b1b5f30b2670a27a14ee56599f5a565408a788c49e2edde48722f3480", "semantic_review_status": "pass"}}
